// Runa at Merrow's End (bible 4.1's hold option, "needs Emberdown"; character-bibles.md §3, §9): asked at the bell in
// Act 2 (Bell_Runa_Named), she comes to the coast to count a fish village. Unwalked, she teaches the walk here for a
// Wren who never learned it, and leads it; walked, she puts Merrow's End in the roll-call. She stands by Dotha's stoop
// while asked for (FlagPresence), and not at all once the village was let go.

title: Merrow_Runa
---
<<if walked("Saltmarrow_B")>>
    <<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.runa.counted_merrow")>>
        <<sing runa>>
        Runa: Forty-two, Wren. Forty-three, Dotha. Forty-four, the water, since it listens. #face:bright #line:089c430
        Runa: A fish village in the roll-call. Mother would've laughed. Then she'd have counted it too. #face:bright #line:02399ed
        <<flag saltmarrow.runa.counted_merrow 1>>
    <<else>>
        Runa: Forty-three, Dotha. She hums along now. Doesn't know the words. Nobody does, down here. #still #face:bright #line:0c704bc
    <<endif>>
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("saltmarrow.runa.came")>>
    Runa: Said we'd walk it. The coast is a long way to carry a bell. I brought the tune. #face:bright #line:0b9c894
    Runa: Nine songs. She sang me the weather one. Short. We'll put a street to each. #line:016589f
    <<flag saltmarrow.runa.came 1>>
<<else>>
    Runa: Still nine. Still not walked. The tide's done more rounds than we have. #still #face:grave #line:0705f4d
<<endif>>
-> Walk it. All of it. #line:0ab7820
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Runa: Stand where I say, when I say it. Dotha's stoop first. Everything starts at somebody's door. #face:bright #line:01d21d2
    <<flag holdfast.walk_learned 1>>
    <<walk merrows_end>>
-> Where does it start? #line:05f2509
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Runa: Her stoop, the post, the shaft's foot, the step. Then back by the steps. Two verses. Short village. #still #line:0a98950
-> ... #line:008b085
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Runa: Not tonight, then. The tide keeps the beat till you're ready. It's patient. We're not. #still #line:0b17e76
===
